John McCarthy (1956) - first talked about AI during a conference that he organized
Alan Turing Mathison - Used AI to build Bombe Machines that deciphered Nazi coded messages from the Enigma machine during world war ii
	* AI finds it difficult to solve problems that are intuitive to humans: 
		- telling whether a friend is angry or not
		- differentiating between items
		- taking notes
Symbolic AI - AI systems with hard coded rules used to solve well-defined tasks and complex problems
	- Couldn't do
		- image recognition, object detection, object segmentation, language translation, natural language processing tasks 
			ML and DL were designed to solve these tasks
			
AI --> ML --> DL
